<title>USA: Mohave 750 MW coal-fired unit seen up Tues night.</title>
<headline>Mohave 750 MW coal-fired unit seen up Tues night.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 750 megawatt (MW) unit 2 at the Mohave coal-fired power plant near Laughlin, Nev., was expected to restart around 1900 to 2000 PST on Tuesday, a spokesman at the plant said.</p>
<p>The unit was taken off-line late Saturday to repair a leaking boiler tube.</p>
<p>Mohave's other 750 MW unit was operating at 669 MW due to a lack of demand for power, the spokesman noted.</p>
<p>Southern California Edison Co is the majority owner and operator of the Mohave units.</p>
<p>--D Beasley, Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
